{"name":"Blueprint","hex":"#35637c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blueprint","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of paper-based reproduction process producing white-on-blue images by means of a photosensitive ferric compound, used primarily for technical and architecture's drawings, now largely replaced by other technologies.","A print produced with this process."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a blueprint for.","To make a detailed operational plan for; to design or plan out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blueprint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blueprint","blocks":[{"text":"A blueprint is a reproduction of a technical drawing or engineering drawing using a contact print process on light-sensitive sheets introduced by Sir John Herschel in 1842. The traditional white-on-blue appearance of blueprints is a result of the cyanotype process, which allowed rapid and accurate production of an unlimited number of copies of an original reference. It was widely used for over a century for the reproduction of specification drawings used in construction and industry. Blueprints are characterized by white lines on a blue background, a negative of the original. Color or shades of grey cannot be reproduced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/AcotacionTecnico.svg/330px-AcotacionTecnico.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blueprint","wikidata":"Q422321"},{"title":"Blueprint (rapper)","blocks":[{"text":"Albert Andrew Shepard, better known by his stage name Blueprint, is an American rapper and record producer from Columbus, Ohio. He is a founder of Weightless Recordings."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blueprint_(rapper)","wikidata":"Q4930408"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/John_C._Butler-class_destroyer_escort_outboard_profile%2C_29_September_1944_%282